# Parakeet dictation server (local, GPU) — the hand-edited source.
#
# requirements.txt beside it is generated from this file: every dependency
# pinned to an exact version with its artifact hashes, so `docker build` today
# and next month install the same tree, and a compromised upstream release
# fails the hash check instead of landing silently. Edit here, then run:
#
#   ./scripts/lock-requirements.sh
#
# ---- why torch is pinned here but excluded from the lock ----
#
# The Dockerfile installs torch from the PyTorch cu130 index *before* this file,
# because those wheels bundle the CUDA + cuDNN runtime. It must not be installed
# again from PyPI, which would clobber the cu130 build with a generic one — so
# torch, triton and the nvidia-* runtime packages that come with it are resolved
# (to keep the rest of the tree consistent with them) and then omitted from the
# output. See scripts/lock-requirements.sh for the exclusion list.
#
# The pin below exists purely so the resolver knows which torch will be present.
# Without it the resolution drifts to whatever PyPI's newest torch is — 2.13.0
# at the time of writing — and pins everything else against a torch the image
# never installs. Keep this in lockstep with the Dockerfile's cu130 install.
torch==2.12.1

